    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="1219" n="1205" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.71114A/9–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-16T00:00:00-04:00">September 16,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2228. ReDeptel 2148, September 7. Department is informed by Legation Bern<anchor
                        n="54" xml:id="d739-f1"/> that Swiss Legation Bucharest has reported that
                    American colony in Rumania desires learn when representatives of this Government
                    will arrive to protect United States interests vis-à-vis the Soviet
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>From another source<anchor n="55" xml:id="d739-f2"/> Department learns of feeling
                    by approximately 500 Americans in Rumania that they require further protection.
                    Department is requesting Bern<anchor n="56" xml:id="d739-f3"/> to ascertain from
                    Swiss Legation Bucharest exactly what if any obstacles prevent normal extension
                    of protection to Americans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
